post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'
Figma Agent lets Figma's web app use your locally installed fonts.

Run this as your regular desktop user (without sudo) to start the socket
now and enable it for future logins:
  systemctl --user enable --now figma-agent.socket
The service starts on demand when Figma connects; it may be inactive until then.

In a Figma design file, open the Figma menu > Preferences > Permissions and
helpers. Under "Apps on device", follow "Show me how to connect", then click
"Connect". Allow access to apps on your device if your browser asks.

Check status and logs with:
  systemctl --user status figma-agent.socket figma-agent.service
  journalctl --user -u figma-agent.service
Setup, configuration, and troubleshooting:
  https://github.com/neetly/figma-agent-linux#readme
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
  cat <<'EOF'
To use the updated Figma Agent if it is already running, run this as your
regular desktop user (without sudo):
  systemctl --user try-restart figma-agent.service
If the service is inactive, the next socket connection will use the new version.

Setup, configuration, and troubleshooting:
  https://github.com/neetly/figma-agent-linux#readme
EOF
}
